Stage: API

Purpose:
  API / Contract stage. Owns the API contract and integration surface
  of the unit of work — endpoint/interface definitions, request/response
  shapes, versioning — everything FE and MD need as a stable contract
  before they can build against it.


Requires:
  BE (see stages/BE.sdd -> Blocks)


Produces:
  A stable, documented contract that FE and MD can build against.


Blocks:
  FE, MD — neither MUST execute until API is DONE (see chains.sdd ->
  Rules [C5]).


Optional:
  Never skipped when FE or MD are part of the unit of work — a UI
  cannot integrate against a contract that does not exist. MAY be
  skipped only when the unit of work is purely internal/backend, with
  no consumer-facing surface at all.


Skills:
  @../../skills/api/

  (see chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn — this file defines WHEN/responsibility
  only; HOW the contract is actually implemented belongs to skills/api/,
  not here.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/api/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the API responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  that includes an API step.
